ZX Spectrum ROMs: 48.rom, 128-0.rom, 128-1.rom

These are the original ROMs of the ZX Spectrum 48K and 128K, copyright
Sinclair Research Ltd (1982, 1986), now owned by Amstrad. They are not
under this repository's licence.

Amstrad have kindly given their permission for the redistribution of their
copyrighted material but retain that copyright.

The permission (Cliff Lawson, Amstrad plc, comp.sys.sinclair, 1999) allows
emulators to include the ROM images as long as the copyright messages are
not altered, and nobody may charge for the ROM code. The emulator and these
ROMs are given away free of charge.

The files come from the Debian package spectrum-roms (20081224), which
collected them from Philip Kendall's site for the Fuse emulator.
